Sentence-final periods produce the strongest negative quote response. Curly
opening quotes also respond to commas, colons and line breaks; ordinary ASCII
quotes need stronger evidence of an opening, rather than closing, use. Code
escapes are quiet. Long dashes at line starts are a related dialogue signal.
